<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xuanzong of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 713–741</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Tang Emperor Xuanzong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xuanzong was an emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> (r. 713–741) whose era is remembered as a cultural and political high point. Tang power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and on the steppe frontier, including relations with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a>, reached its height in his time. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a>, which broke out later in his rule, began the dynasty's long decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-xuanzong-of-tang.jpg" alt="Emperor Xuanzong of Tang" width="320" height="356" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9D%8E%E9%9A%86%E5%9F%BA%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
